<newsitem itemid="493291" id="root" date="1997-04-08" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kohler half year rises, div up.</title>
<headline>Kohler half year rises, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Feb 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     24.8	  vs 22.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 7.0	   vs 6.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share for the six months to end-February rising to within a narrow 24.0 to 24.6 cents band, with consensus at 24.4 cents.</p>
<p>The dividend was seen at between 7.4 and 8.5 cents a share, with consensus at 7.9 cents.  </p>
<p>    Pre-excep attrib income   73.4    vs 64.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   105.5	 vs 97.4</p>
<p>    Tax rate  (pct)	 28.1	  vs 31.6</p>
<p>    Financing costs	 1.3 gain    vs 4.0 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,231.9     vs 1,174.5</p>
<p>Full name: Kohler Ltd (packaging)</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains     2.5	   vs 1.1</p>
<p>NOTE - The fim gave no dividend date details.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
